course: dictionary
lesson: 6112
title: Names, slang and playground teasing
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Mickey is a name. It is short for Michael, and it is also the name of Mickey Mouse, the famous cartoon mouse from Disney. A name starts with a capital letter, so a capital M usually means a person or a character.
explain: In British, Irish and Australian playground talk, «stop taking the mickey» means stop teasing. To take the mickey out of someone means to make fun of them. Read the context: is it friendly joking, or is it hurting someone? Teasing that hurts is unkind.
explain: Mickey Mouse can also be an adjective meaning silly, small or not serious, as in a Mickey Mouse job. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Mickey is a first name, short for Michael.
fact: Mickey Mouse is the famous cartoon mouse from Disney.
fact: To take the mickey (UK, informal) means to tease someone or make fun of them.
fact: Mickey Mouse, as an adjective, means silly, small or not serious.
fact: Teasing that hurts someone is unkind, and teachers deal with it.
exercise: Mickey with a capital M is the name of a famous cartoon mouse. Who is he? | A kind of sweet | *A cartoon mouse from Disney | A playground game | A school bell
exercise: «Stop taking the mickey.» What does this mean? | Stop singing | Stop running | Stop drawing mice | *Stop teasing
exercise: Rhea says her homework was a Mickey Mouse job. What does she mean? | It was homework about mice | *It was silly and not very serious | It was long and very hard | It was a job at a theme park
test: «He keeps taking the mickey out of my new coat, and it is not funny.» What does taking the mickey mean here? | Cleaning a coat | Giving someone a present | *Teasing someone in an unkind way | Singing a song
test: Mickey is short for which name? | *Michael | Martin | Mario | Mark
exam: Someone keeps taking the mickey out of a friend. What is the best thing to do? | Laugh loudly and walk away | Hide the friend's bag | Join in and tease the friend more | *Tell them to stop, and tell a teacher if it keeps happening
